    {
      "title": "Modi watches as fighter jets roar across Varanasi skies at IAF air show",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/pm-modi-varanasi-uttar-pradesh-iaf-air-show/article71622977.ece",
      "description": "IAF’s Surya Kiran and Sarang teams perform aerial manoeuvres over the Ganga; PM also inaugurates garment unit expected to generate jobs for women",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-10-25T15:08:17"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sukhoi, Tejas, Prachand headline IAF's grand air show in Varanasi",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/sukhoi-tejas-prachand-headline-iaf-s-grand-air-show-in-varanasi-126102500274_1.html",
      "description": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Sunday attended the Indian Air Force's air show 'Wings over Ganges' at Namo Ghat in Varanasi and witnessed a display of aerial manoeuvres by the IAF's premier display teams.\nDefence Minister Rajnath Singh, Uttar Pradesh Governor Anandiben Patel and Chief Minister Yogi Adityanath accompanied Modi on the final day of the three-day air show held to commemorate the 94th anniversary of the Indian Air Force.\nAccording to Air Force officials, the show features fighter aircraft, including the Sukhoi-30 MKI, indigenous Tejas and LCH Prachand, along with helicopter displays.\nThree Kiran aircraft flew in a 'V' formation, creating a spectacle in the colours of the national flag, while Mi-17 helicopters carrying the tricolour participated in the Omkar formation.\nThe Surya Kiran aerobatic team showcased precision flying and coordinated manoeuvres, while the Sarang helicopter display team enthralled spectators with its aerial stunts.\nModi's presence at the event .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-25T08:58:00"
    }
  ]
